      "scope": "Design before C repair. Resolved-IR source-projected executable composition of retained-slot join/GC/reuse and tagged acknowledged result distribution, with one extra retained nonzero requester. Shrink three to two, then grow two to three; the new member must consume the growth result before body execution and shutdown. At most one join failure followed by recovery and weak fairness remain progress assumptions; preserving the recovered error as first status is a proposed policy, not current Gambit semantics. Extra peer participates in result acknowledgement, not a full native GC/barrier implementation. Nested-import conversion and namespace failures are archived as tool/model construction DENYs, not algorithm counterexamples. No permanent-failure recovery, C result protocol/refinement, arbitrary membership, native GC/bootstrap/Gerbil or release admission."
